[1.276033,"o","\u001b[?2026h\u001b[2J\u001b[H\u001b[3J                                                                                                                        \u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n The Lab already has all four queens21 shape plays, so the first intent will specify a controlled rerun of those arms:  \u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n three repetitions each, with infrastructure failures kept out of the research results. I’m applying the Lab’s current  \u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n play-authoring skill, particularly its rules for sourced problems, independent checks, and no winner claim from an     \u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n invalid comparison.                                                                                                    \u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n                                                                                                                        \u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n For the second intent, I’m choosing the Erdős minimum-overlap problem: search for a better construction during one     \u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n three-hour Codex run, with a score recomputed from the construction itself. A newer paper improves on the well-known   \u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n TTT-Discover result, so that older result cannot be the acceptance bar. The intent will require a current, replayed    \u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n incumbent before a spend card.                                                                                         \u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n                                                                                                                        \u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n The drafts will address two risks: the original queens workload may be too large for a fair two-hour comparison, and   \u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n overlap search can reward a normalization error instead of a better construction. I’ll require workload calibration    \u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n for the first and exact rational scoring for the second. This adds two local Markdown intents only; proof fixtures,    \u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n live admission checks, costs, and preflight will remain explicitly pending.                                            \u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n                                                                                                                        \u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n Two details matter for the rerun: the existing swarm16 play says its 16 workers cannot all be alive together, and      \u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n peers3 uses separate stores with mail despite wording about a shared store. The intent will make both conditions       \u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n explicit and block a mislabeled comparison. For overlap, I also found a reported normalization defect in a newer       \u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n headline result; the future checker must derive the bin count from the submitted vector and verify every signed lag.   \u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n                                                                                                                        \u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n Saved both **unapproved intents**, each with a review card and remaining preparation:                                  \u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n                                                                                                                        \u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n | Intent | Review proposal |                                                                                           \u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n |---|---|                                                                                                              \u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n | [queens21-shapes-rerun-20261015a](intents/queens21-shapes-rerun-20261015a.md) | Three repetitions each of solo,      \u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n tree4, swarm16 and peers3; two hours per trial. Proposes calibrated 19-queens sizing and treats infrastructure         \u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n failures as missing data. Flags swarm concurrency and peer-store semantics. |                                          \u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n | [erdos-overlap-steering-20261015a](intents/erdos-overlap-steering-20261015a.md) | One three-hour Codex run seeking a \u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n better Erdős minimum-overlap construction, with exact scoring and a future prediction-based steering checkpoint. |     \u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n                                                                            "]
